Subject: [PATCH 3/4] test(smf): cover the NAS encoding of the Modification
 Command
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds test_nas_modification_command.cpp, which encodes the IEs the N1 builders
assemble — the smf_n1 builders themselves need the global SMF context, so
they cannot be unit-tested directly.

Asserts that a DELETE QoS rule is the 4 octets with a length indicator of one
that Table 9.11.4.13.1@3GPP TS 24.501 describes, that what a QoS rule reports
as its length is what it encodes, that Encode() refuses a buffer smaller than
the IE, that the removal and creation cases of the PDU Session Modification
Command both encode to exactly GetLength() octets, that Session-AMBR, the
authorized QoS rules and the authorized QoS flow descriptions each carry
their IEI, and that the encoded message decodes again.

Extends test_session_handler.cpp with the rule the handler actually builds,
and with the case where no edge supplies a rule identifier.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
